multiview-stage3.patch — gl_ViewID_OVR/gl_Layer in the MSL translator
===================================================================
(stage 3 of the multiview plan of the Vice City port)

Base:        ANGLE e4499e6b2835a6996507f1b99920bc56f0122573
Order:       apply after klepton.patch, angle-metal-fixes.patch and
             multiview-stage2.patch.
State:       stage 3 (2026-09-23), verified at the desk: both a minimal
             shader AND the real librw skin shader (with the port's
             injections) translate to the instanced emulation, and the
             generated MSL compiles with xcrun metal without errors. Takes
             effect at runtime only with stage 4 (draw wiring: double the
             instance count, fill ANGLE_multiviewBaseViewLayerIndex).

Three fixes of the same class — multiview symbols escaped the MSL pipeline
collection:

1. TranslatorMSL.cpp: gl_Layer (written by the instanced multiview
   emulation) is declared as a builtin as soon as it appears in the tree —
   before, the emitter referenced a symbol that was never declared.
2. Pipeline.cpp: EvqLayerOut moves into the VertexOut struct;
   EvqEmulatedViewIDOVR (ViewID_OVR) into the NonConstGlobals — otherwise
   they become mutable program globals, which Metal rejects.
3. EmitMetal.cpp: gl_Layer gets [[render_target_array_index]] and is
   declared as uint32_t (Metal requires unsigned; the emulation's int
   assignment converts implicitly).

Device precondition (gate, 2026-09-23, PASS 18/18): rate map + layer routing
via render_target_array_index per instance + memoryless MSAA work together
(VC_MV_SPIKE=3, MultiviewSpike.swift in the app).

diff --git a/src/compiler/translator/msl/EmitMetal.cpp b/src/compiler/translator/msl/EmitMetal.cpp
index 014df1fe73..0ed7d55cf6 100644
--- a/src/compiler/translator/msl/EmitMetal.cpp
+++ b/src/compiler/translator/msl/EmitMetal.cpp
@@ -836,6 +836,14 @@ void GenMetalTraverser::emitPostQualifier(const EmitVariableDeclarationConfig &e
             mOut << " [[point_size]]";
             break;
 
+        case TQualifier::EvqLayerOut:
+            // VC multiview (Stufe 3): route the instanced-multiview emulation's
+            // gl_Layer into the target slice. Metal requires an unsigned type
+            // for this attribute; the declaration type is overridden to
+            // uint32_t in emitVariableDeclaration.
+            mOut << " [[render_target_array_index]]";
+            break;
+
         case TQualifier::EvqVertexID:
             if (evdConfig.isMainParameter)
             {
@@ -1568,7 +1576,19 @@ void GenMetalTraverser::emitVariableDeclaration(const VarDecl &decl,
         default:
         {
             ASSERT(symbolType != SymbolType::Empty || evdConfig.isParameter);
-            emitOrdinaryVariableDeclaration(decl, evdConfig);
+            // VC multiview (Stufe 3): gl_Layer is int in GLSL, but Metal's
+            // [[render_target_array_index]] attribute requires an unsigned
+            // type. Emit the DECLARATION as uint32_t; the int expression the
+            // multiview emulation assigns converts implicitly (C++ rules).
+            if (type.getQualifier() == TQualifier::EvqLayerOut)
+            {
+                mOut << "uint32_t ";
+                emitNameOf(decl);
+            }
+            else
+            {
+                emitOrdinaryVariableDeclaration(decl, evdConfig);
+            }
         }
     }
 
